    "windows-gfx1101": {
      "state": "port-ready",
      "blocked": true,
      "blocked_reason": "Never Windows-ported (even for CUDA): zero _WIN32 guards in csrc/. The ROCm/HIP GPU kernels hipify cleanly (0 unsupported CUDA calls), but csrc/mem_alloc.cpp (the c_ops host allocator) includes <linux/mman.h>/<linux/mempolicy.h> and uses mmap/NUMA/hugepage/shm pinned allocators with no Windows equivalent. First build error: bitmap.cpp __builtin_popcount/__builtin_ctz undefined in MSVC. Windows GPU validation requires a full Win32 host-layer port (VirtualAlloc+large-pages+Win32-shared-memory) that is separate from and out of scope for the ROCm port. Same root cause as gfx1151 block. gfx90a/gfx1100 (Linux) validated.",
      "validated_sha": null,
